## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/solvepoisson.html
- Summary (EN): Solve Poisson computes a solution to Poisson's equation for a single-channel (mono) layer, using the rhs input as the right-hand side. The solve is limited to a region defined by a signed distance field.
- Résumé (FR) : Solve Poisson résout l'équation de Poisson sur un calque mono, à l'intérieur d'une région délimitée par un champ de distance signé.

- Inputs meaning: ["rhs (required): mono layer holding the right side of Poisson's equation", "boundary (required): mono signed distance field defining the solve region, values <= 0 are inside", "dirichlet (optional): prescribed solution values on the boundary", "neumann (optional): prescribed normal-derivative values on the boundary", "blend (optional): per-pixel mix between Dirichlet and Neumann conditions", "initial (optional): starting estimate for the solution"]

- Key parameters: ["Iterations: solver iteration count, more is more converged but slower", "Boundary Blend: global mix between Dirichlet (0) and Neumann (1), overridden by a connected blend input", "Pre-conditioner Iterations: pre-conditioner passes during the solve", "Smoothing Iterations: smoothing passes inside the pre-conditioner", "Coarsest Smoothing Iterations: smoothing passes at the coarsest level, used in place of an exact coarse solve"]

- Caveats: ["A connected blend input overrides the Boundary Blend parameter", "Boundary sign convention matters: a mis-signed distance field solves over the wrong area", "Raising iteration counts improves accuracy at the cost of cook time", "Distinct from Solve Poisson Multigrid, which solves over a rectangular layer"]

